<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prekmurje</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prekmurje is the north-easternmost region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, lying beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mur-river">Mura</a> river on the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murska-sobota">Murska Sobota</a>. It belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> for most of its history and had a Slovene-speaking majority, a Hungarian minority and a large Lutheran population. Yugoslav troops occupied it in August 1919, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon">Treaty of Trianon</a> assigned it to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prekmurje.jpg" alt="Prekmurje" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iswoar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landscape_Gori%C4%8Dko_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
